                            <comment id="15190527" author="felixcheung" created="Fri, 11 Mar 2016 06:34:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is because to capture output, sys.stdout is replaced from the code in zeppelin_pyspark.py&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;output = Logger()
sys.stdout = output
sys.stderr = output
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15190530" author="felixcheung" created="Fri, 11 Mar 2016 06:37:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;According to this, &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.python.org/2/library/sys.html#sys.stdout&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://docs.python.org/2/library/sys.html#sys.stdout&lt;/a&gt;, the replacement is only required to have a `write` method.&lt;br/&gt;
I guess here, multiprocessing, is expecting a flush method too.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
